# MaAI Environment Configuration — copy to .env and fill in as needed.
# MaAI has no backend and no required external credentials to run: every
# core workflow (auth, camera, OCR, voice, risk engine, alerts, referrals)
# works fully offline with zero configuration.

# Display name used in a few UI strings.
EXPO_PUBLIC_APP_NAME=MaAI

# Optional — AI-assisted validation/explanation backend proxy.
# See services/ai/aiValidationService.ts and docs/AI_PIPELINE.md.
# Leave unset to run with the deterministic risk engine and OCR field
# extraction only (the default, and the fully-working experience today).
#
# If set, this MUST point at YOUR OWN backend endpoint — never at a provider
# API directly. A client app (mobile or web) cannot safely hold a real LLM
# provider API key: anything shipped in client JS can be read by opening the
# bundle. Your backend endpoint should hold the real provider key
# server-side and this app only ever talks to your endpoint.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_AI_VALIDATION_ENDPOINT=https://your-backend.example.com/ai/validate
